setp('P69',r'''Replication-level contrasts confirmed that jump settings improved training temporal fit but worsened holdout fit (Table~\ref{tab:jump_ablation_uncertainty}). Four seeds supplied $1{,}000$ market replications per window with frozen fits. Naive and corrected composition shared draws; settings reused unchanged asset or market components, while enabled and disabled generators used separate random streams. We averaged each metric across tickers within a replication, differenced settings, and divided the standard deviation of the $1{,}000$ differences by $\sqrt{1{,}000}$; intervals used the mean plus or minus $1.96$ standard errors. This retained shared-market dependence but excluded fitting and historical-window uncertainty. All paths entered the primary scores; $247$ training-length and $22$ holdout-length market paths contained episodes, with enabled asset shares of $24.24\%$ and $2.46\%$. These rare holdout episodes and the transferred SPY calibration limit interpretation; KS non-rejection remains descriptive under temporal dependence.''')
