setp('P74',r'''Pooled one-day tail thresholds used $B=5{,}000$ separately constructed $249$-day paths per asset and method (Table~\ref{tab:var}). Linear empirical quantiles pooled all $249B$ daily log returns. Each replication shared a market path across assets and methods; each asset path retained its centering and scaling rules, with hybrid scaling using training market variance. Hidden Markov models started from their fitted stationary laws with jumps disabled; GARCH retained its $100$-step warmup. Thresholds were calibrated for $423$ training assets ($393$ GARCH fits) before reading holdout data. The estimand is a uniformly selected day in this finite-horizon construction, not cumulative risk.''')
setp('P75',r'''Pools of $100$, $500$, $1{,}000$, $2{,}500$ and $5{,}000$ paths tested numerical stability; $1{,}000$ independent paths checked simulated exceedances. Relative threshold changes divided the difference by the absolute $5{,}000$-path threshold. Doubling $2{,}500$ to $5{,}000$ changed mean observed exceedance rates by less than $0.006$ percentage points. Median absolute relative changes in $99\%$ thresholds were $0.12$--$0.30\%$ across methods, with $95$th percentiles $0.37$--$1.03\%$ and a worst case of $3.95\%$. Independent simulated exceedances were $5.03$--$5.04\%$ and $1.01$--$1.02\%$ against $5\%$ and $1\%$ targets. These checks establish simulation stability, not real-market coverage.''')
